  "text": "We are given:\n\n- Triangle $ ABC $,\n- Line $ m $ passes through the **midpoint** of $ AB $ and is **perpendicular to $ AC $**,\n- Line $ m $ intersects $ BC $ at point $ D $,\n- Area of $ \\triangle ABD = 9 $,\n- Area of $ \\triangle BDC = 4 $,\n- Length of $ BC = 8 $,\n- Find the length of $ AD $.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Use the given areas and lengths to find ratios\n\nLet’s denote:\n\n- $ AB = c $,\n- $ AC = b $,\n- $ BC = a = 8 $,\n- $ D $ is the point where line $ m $ intersects $ BC $,\n- $ AD $ is the segment we need to find.\n\nWe know:\n\n- Area of $ \\triangle ABD = 9 $,\n- Area of $ \\triangle BDC = 4 $,\n- $ BC = 8 $.\n\nSince both triangles share the base $ BC $, their areas are in the same ratio as their heights from $ A $ and $ D $, respectively.\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{Area of } \\triangle ABD}{\\text{Area of } \\triangle BDC} = \\frac{AD}{DC}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{AD}{DC} \\Rightarrow AD = \\frac{9}{4} \\cdot DC\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Express $ AD + DC = BC = 8 $\n\nLet $ DC = x $. Then $ AD = \\frac{9}{4}x $, so:\n\n$$\nAD + DC = \\frac{9}{4}x + x = \\frac{13}{4}x = 8\n\\Rightarrow x = \\frac{32}{13}\n\\Rightarrow AD = \\frac{9}{4} \\cdot \\frac{32}{13} = \\frac{72}{52} = \\frac{18}{13}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\frac{18}{13}}\n$$",
